<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

  <!--
  CompSapientHumanlikeMechHead.cs doesn't exist natively on any ThingDef built on
  Fortified's "HumanlikeMech" rendering system (thingClass Fortified.HumanlikeMech,
  renderTree HumanlikeMech or a mod's own copy of it, plus a Fortified.HumanlikeMechExtension
  carrying the actual head texture) - it's added here so it flows through the same
  clone/whitelist pipeline as the rest of a mech's comps (see compWhitelist in
  HumanlikeAnimalSettings_MechQueens.xml). It self-gates to sapient-only at runtime (see
  IsSapientMech), so its presence on the non-sapient original is harmless - a real
  HumanlikeMech pawn already renders its head correctly through the static tree without
  it.

  Two mods share this exact rendering system so far: Dead Man's Switch's Lady, and
  Ascension Megacorp's Rocky (all five of its PawnKindDef loadouts - AR/LMG/DMR/Heavy -
  share one ThingDef, so a single entry covers all of them). Each mod needs its own
  Operation since PatchOperationAdd's xpath has to name a specific defName - there's no
  way to instead match "any ThingDef carrying Fortified.HumanlikeMechExtension" from XML
  alone. If a third mod turns up using the same system, add another Operation here rather
  than trying to make this one generic.
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="Aoba.DeadManSwitch.Core">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="DMS_Mech_Lady"]/comps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientHumanlikeMechHead" />
    </value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd" MayRequire="AOBA.USAC.Core">
    <xpath>Defs/ThingDef[defName="USAC_Mech_Rocky"]/comps</xpath>
    <value>
      <li Class="SapientMechanoidFix.CompProperties_SapientHumanlikeMechHead" />
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
